  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## The Cav∴lapsum
    
    A catastrophic rupture at Sleek☽ Caemomot, a Nightshelf mining complex, during the Frozen Peace. Deep-ice fissures released ancient pressure-depth energy from strata predating known penguin habitation. Survivors described the sound as splitting bone; light emerged from the fractures — not aurora-glow but something older, compressed into the Berg's deep layers for millennia.
    
    Three mining teams were caught in the surge. Two did not return. The accounts uniformly give forty miners, a number I note without further comment. What was recovered: tools on the cavern floor, a cracked fire-core hammer, unfinished crystal-work. The smell of scorched ice persisted for seasons.
    
    ### The Fawned~ Crypt-seal
    
    From the released energy, something crystallized: The Fawned~ Crypt-seal, a relic of sufficient power that the Nightshelf restructured their legal framework around it. No source I have located explains the mechanism by which raw pressure-depth energy solidified into a discrete artifact.
    
    ### Legal and Memorial Legacy
    
    The institutional response was extraordinary in scope. Laws and covenants born from or commemorating the disaster include Mandatum∴ccord (binding law of witnessed testimony and blood-debt), Umbra∴go (memorial observances), Foedus∴vincu (the Nightshelf's de facto constitution), Iudicium∴culum (emergency judicial decree), Foedus∴sper (covenant of shared witness), Pactum∴silenti, and Signum∴men. That a single mining disaster generated this breadth of reform suggests the Cav∴lapsum exposed institutional vulnerabilities the Nightshelf had long tolerated.
    
    ### The ☽'sanctmocsaecus' Twilight-bells
    
    Accounts diverge. One tradition holds the bells — seven obsidian chimes in a frame of shadow-steel and ancestor bone — were forged from crystal fragments recovered from the rupture. Another states they predated the collapse and were caught in it, two chimes now bearing white stress-fractures. The chronicle "The Twilight-Bells of Silvesiris" places them in a guarded geothermal cavern, retrieved by the shadow-walker Sivruta~ at great cost. These versions cannot all be true simultaneously. The bells exist; their provenance does not survive scrutiny.
    
    ### Unresolved Connections
    
    The Cav∴lapsum is recorded as the catalyst of The Rupture-Song, an orca war-ritual that fractures the user's blood-pressure into concussive waves. How an orca combat technique traces its origin to a Nightshelf mining disaster is not adequately explained by any source I possess.
    
    The fissure site remains sealed. A penguin identified only as Kael — the youngest of the three teams — leaves fire-core tokens at the entrance on the anniversary.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
