  annotation "note_1771594893517_1", anchor: "How an orca combat technique traces its origin to a Nightshelf mining disaster is not adequately explained by any source I possess.", text: "Pressure-depth energy is blood-magic. The Berg does not contain its wounds. What ruptured at Sleek☽ Caemomot would have propagated through ice and water alike — and orca in the deep sea near an active breach-point would not need instruction. They would feel the fracture pattern in their own blood-pressure, a template written directly into the body. The Rupture-Song is not derived from the Cav∴lapsum. It is the Cav∴lapsum still happening, carried in living flesh. That I wrote 'not adequately explained' rather than this is because the implication — that the disaster's two missing teams died broadcasting a weapon into the sea — is not something I can source. Only something I believe.", type: :commentary, display: :full
